Project Title
Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer
2. Existing System
The school IT helpdesk receives multiple support requests from students and teachers for issues such as network connectivity, hardware failures, account access problems, and system performance issues.
Currently, IT staff manually review each ticket to identify the issue type, select the appropriate category and subcategory, and inform the caller about ticket creation.
This manual process is time-consuming, error-prone, and difficult to scale when the number of requests increases. �
Auto Ticket Classification using Flow Designer.pdf
3. Proposed System
The proposed system uses ServiceNow Flow Designer to automatically classify IT tickets when they are created.
The system analyzes keywords in the ticket's short description and description fields and automatically assigns the appropriate Category and Subcategory.
It also sends an automated email notification to the caller after ticket creation.
4. Functional Requirements
The system must:
Automatically classify IT tickets based on the issue description.
Assign the appropriate Category without manual intervention.
Assign the appropriate Subcategory without manual intervention.
Support dependent choice logic between Category and Subcategory.
Send an automated email notification to the caller upon ticket creation.
Store ticket information in a structured and standardized format. �
